# Stitch `DESIGN.md` — read before building UI

Treat `DESIGN.md` as canonical UI/design guidance unless the user overrides it.

## Discovery

```bash
git ls-files "**/DESIGN.md" 2>/dev/null || find . -name DESIGN.md -not -path '*/node_modules/*'
```

If multiple files exist, use the one nearest the edited subtree.

## When this applies

- Components/pages/layout/theme/token changes
- Styling work (CSS/Tailwind/design tokens)
- Design-related rule authoring (`/create-rule`, `.mdc`)

## If `DESIGN.md` is missing

Note it briefly, follow existing UI code/rules, and offer creating one via `design-md` if relevant.
